  "summary_en": "Opinion of the EU Committee of the Regions on the Commission's 'Artificial Intelligence for Europe' communication. It supports a common European approach, more investment, ethical guidelines and urgent legislative proposals, and stresses the role of local and regional authorities, digital skills and retraining. Robotics is mentioned only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Supports the Commission's AI strategy and calls for urgent European-level legislative proposals",
   "Regrets the strategy is not binding on Member States and that the proposed funding is insufficient",
   "Calls for local and regional authorities to be involved in AI investment and ecosystems",
   "Calls for retraining and digital skills programmes to avoid inequality",
   "Insists privacy and individual rights be guaranteed as AI develops"
